NAME:
   feedwatch - agent-first watcher for RSS and Atom feeds

USAGE:
   feedwatch [global options] [command [command options]]

COMMANDS:
   migrate   apply or inspect schema migrations
   poll      poll due feeds (or the named feeds) and report new items
   check     validate feed reachability and parseability without storing items or updating state
   add       subscribe to an explicit feed URL after validating it parses as a feed
   list      list subscriptions with status, alias, tags, failure count, and last error
   rm        unsubscribe a feed by URL or unique alias, or a whole lane by tag, removing their stored items
   enable    re-enable a disabled feed and reset its failure lifecycle so it is due again
   disable   disable a feed so poll skips it until re-enabled
   tag       read or edit the tags on a subscription
   tags      list every tag in use with the number of feeds carrying it
   items     query stored item history with filters, ordering, and pagination
   prune     trim stored item history by age and/or per-feed count, preserving dedup
   discover  list candidate feeds autodiscovered or probed from a URL (read-only)
   import    add subscriptions from an OPML outline read from a file or stdin
   export    export subscriptions as OPML 2.0 to a file or stdout
   schema    emit the machine-readable interface contract
   help, h   Shows a list of commands or help for one command

GLOBAL OPTIONS:
   --db PATH                   store location: a filesystem PATH or a postgres:// DSN [$FEEDWATCH_DB]
   --format FORMAT             output FORMAT: json or text (default: "json") [$FEEDWATCH_FORMAT]
   --log-level LEVEL           log LEVEL: error, warn, info, or debug (default: "info")
   --quiet                     raise the log floor to errors only
   --no-color                  disable color in text output
   --user-agent string         HTTP User-Agent header (default: "feedwatch") [$FEEDWATCH_USER_AGENT]
   --concurrency int           worker pool size for concurrent polling (default: 8) [$FEEDWATCH_CONCURRENCY]
   --connect-timeout duration  dial deadline per feed (default: 5s)
   --timeout duration          overall deadline per feed (default: 30s)
   --proxy URL                 outbound HTTP proxy URL
   --ca-bundle FILE            path to a custom CA bundle FILE
   --min-tls VERSION           minimum TLS VERSION: 1.2 or 1.3 (default: "1.2")
   --allow-private             allow redirects into private address space
   --version, -v               print version information
   --help, -h                  show help
